From: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:58:12 +0200
Subject: [parser] Check IsIdentifier for `for (async of ...)` restriction

In `ParseForStatement`, `for (async of ...)` is disallowed by checking
whether the parsed LHS expression is `async`. Previously, this check
only tested `scanner()->current_token() == Token::kAsync &&
!scanner()->literal_contains_escapes()`, which was true whenever the
last consumed token of the LHS expression was `async`.

As a result, valid loops such as `for (x.async of [1]) {}` were
rejected with `SyntaxError: The left-hand side of a for-of loop may not
be 'async'`, and invalid LHS expressions ending in `async` (such as
`for (+async of [1]) {}` or `for (a, async of [1]) {}`) reported the
wrong error message.

Also check `impl()->IsIdentifier(expression)` when computing
`expression_is_async`.

Bug: 567222737
